atlas forms

architecture form-graph
  canonical_name FormGraph
  family forms
  domain Forms
  layer forms
  semantic_question What is the structure of this human-boundary form, independent of any one submission?
  purpose The form as a graph -- fields, dependencies, evidence slots, attachments, approvals -- distinct from AtomicForm, which compiles it against state.
  maturity implemented
  node_types FormNode
  node_types FieldNode
  node_types FieldDependency
  edge_types field_depends_on
  edge_types required_when
  internal_calculus conditional-requirement resolution against values
  invariant AtomicForm = compile(FormGraph, state), never AtomicForm == FormGraph
  invariant a conditionally-required field is a blocker only when its condition holds
  forbidden_inference AtomicForm == FormGraph
  forbidden_inference a field in the graph -> a field required for this submission
  native_format graf
  source_path lib/libbonfyre/src/bf_form.c
  source_path lib/libbonfyre/include/bf_form.h
  source_path schemas/control/form-graph.cue
  source_path components/BonfyreControlPlane/form_graph.py.archive
  witness lib/libbonfyre/tests/form_test.c: conditional requiredness resolved from values, verified-only autofill (an asserted actor never fills), exact blockers for empty fields, evidence, authority and review gate, ready only when all are satisfied, malformed graphs refused (make -C lib/libbonfyre test-form PASS 2026-11-08); ported from the archived Python on the same actor_nodes table
  witness components/BonfyreControlPlane/tests/test_form_graph.py.archive
  source_lineage SEED-A recursive organ document
  known_gap the native compile is a library in libbonfyre; no organ, page or MCP tool compiles a real form through it yet
architecture atomic-form
  canonical_name AtomicForm
  family forms
  domain Forms
  layer forms/compile
  semantic_question Is this form submit-ready, and if not, exactly what blocks it?
  purpose compile(FormGraph, institutional/actor/evidence/capability/economic/authority state, purpose) -> obligation machine. Fields autofill only from VERIFIED actors; never self-submits.
  maturity implemented
  node_types Field
  node_types EvidenceSlot
  node_types SubmitReadiness
  edge_types autofills_from
  edge_types backed_by
  invariant a field autofills only from a VERIFIED actor
  invariant submit_ready returns exact blockers; never a false green
  invariant the form never crosses the human submit line
  forbidden_inference asserted-via-email actor -> verified_for(profile) autofill
  forbidden_inference evidence slot filled by position -> evidence requirement satisfied
  command BonfyreBrief
  source_path lib/libbonfyre/src/bf_form.c
  source_path lib/libbonfyre/include/bf_form.h
  source_path schemas/control/form-graph.cue
  source_path components/BonfyreControlPlane/atomic_forms.py.archive
  source_path components/BonfyreControlPlane/institution_loop.py.archive
  witness lib/libbonfyre/tests/form_test.c: conditional requiredness resolved from values, verified-only autofill (an asserted actor never fills), exact blockers for empty fields, evidence, authority and review gate, ready only when all are satisfied, malformed graphs refused (make -C lib/libbonfyre test-form PASS 2026-11-08); ported from the archived Python on the same actor_nodes table
  witness components/BonfyreControlPlane/tests/test_atomic_forms.py.archive
  witness components/BonfyreControlPlane/tests/test_institution_loop.py.archive
  source_lineage AtomicForm human-boundary compiler
  known_gap the native compile is a library in libbonfyre; no organ, page or MCP tool compiles a real form through it yet
